  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1205 PM CDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nA persistence strategy, steady-as-she-goes approach is best in \nthe near term with our continued high pressure dominated \nforecast. That means daily highs around 80F thru Friday, a good\ndozen or so degrees above climatological norms. Mild lows will\nrun 5-10F above climo., bottoming out in the upper 40s to lower\n50s.\n\nRain chances make their emergence in the forecast this weekend,\nwhich heralds a wetter period extending into next week with\ndaily rain chances prevailing. The first half of the weekend\nstill looks dry, with most model members holding off on\nappreciable rain chances til Saturday night (and Sunday). The\nchance occurs coincident with the opening up and flattening out\nof a weak wave of low pressure that makes its way across the MS\nValley over the course of the weekend. With little instability \nto tap, we're looking at probably 1/2 inch or less cumulative \nrainfall totals, mostly in the 06z-18z Sunday time frame; a \nlittle before and a little after not-withstanding.\n\nA brief pause/lull in chances occurs starting out the new week,\nbefore a broad synoptic low winds out of the Rockies and Plains\nstates and tracks our direction. Its current tracking takes the\nparent low center to our south, which is pinched on both sides \nby high pressure ridging in an inverted omega-like blocking \nlook to the pattern; the net effect will be more clouds/pcpn \nchances daily and temperatures a little closer to seasonal norms\nwith highs in the lower 70s. The further southward dive of the \nlow means rain totals on this morning's 12Z runs have basically \nhalved from the previous runs...but we still may end up \nverifying the projected \"above normal\" rainfall for the period \nwith the daily rain chances continuing. Best such chances at \nthis time look to be Tuesday into Wednesday.",
